  },
  {
   "finding_id": "err-4",
   "title": "[R4:err-4] A transient MusicBrainz outage is flattened to None by CoverArtFallback's outer except, and resolve() caches that None as the album's FALLBACK payload for the whole session",
   "body": "_Round 4 cold audit (2026-08-07) · finding `err-4` · **Wave 2 — Write-path integrity & the error taxonomy** · verdict **CONFIRMED** (executed reproduction) · severity **MEDIUM**_\n\n**Location:** `src/metadata/resolver.py:172`  \n**Lens:** Error handling, resilience & cross-fix interaction\n\n## Defect\nThe #175 fix taught CoverArtFallback's inner loop to use is_transient(): a NetworkError re-raises to the outer handler 'instead of hammering a dead service' (coverart.py:68-88). But the outer handler (coverart.py:92-96) then converts BOTH transient and permanent outcomes to the same return value, None — destroying the classification the taxonomy just computed. resolve() Step 3 cannot tell 'MusicBrainz is down right now' from 'this album verifiably has no cover art', and caches (FALLBACK, None) whenever the two Discogs tiers completed cleanly (resolver.py:171-172) — with no TTL, so the album is pinned coverless for the rest of the session even after MusicBrainz recovers seconds later. This violates the module's own headline rule ('Transient — ...the album must stay retryable and uncached', errors.py:7-8) for the one tier the rule's plumbing doesn't reach: the resolver threads discogs_completed through both Discogs tiers precisely to avoid caching on a transient, but grants the cover-art tier no equivalent signal. Composition bug between #175's classify-and-reraise and the v1.3.3 fallback-caching rule: each individually correct, composed they cache a transient negative.\n\n## Failure scenario\nA record not in the Discogs collection or database (private pressing, obscure release) starts playing during a brief MusicBrainz outage or 503 rate-limit window. Track 1's cover lookup fails transiently; resolve() caches (FALLBACK, None). Tracks 2-10 hit the album cache and never retry, so the display shows the coverless empty-art card for the entire session — typically until the daily restart — even though MusicBrainz was back before track 2.\n\n## Suggested fix\nLet get_cover_art_url distinguish outcomes: re-raise transient errors (or return a sentinel) from the outer handler, and in resolve() Step 3 wrap the executor call in try/except is_transient — on transient, return the FALLBACK TrackMetadata but skip _cache_store (mirroring discogs_completed), so the next track retries; cache None only on a clean 'searched, no art exists'.\n\n## Verifier's fix note\nThe suggested fix is sound; prefer the re-raise variant over a sentinel: narrow the outer except in get_cover_art_url so is_transient errors propagate (keep catch-and-None for everything else), then in resolve() Step 3 wrap the executor call in try/except, and on is_transient(e) set cover_url=None but skip _cache_store even if discogs_completed — exactly mirroring the discogs_completed pattern. Two details: (1) keep caching None on the clean paths (empty release-list, all candidates exhausted) — that negative cache is correct and load-bearing for MB rate limits; (2) per #175's documented taxonomy, ResponseError/AuthenticationError from search_releases stay permanent and cacheable — don't widen the transient set while fixing this. Add the missing test to test_resolver_error_no_cache.py: coverart raising NetworkError with clean Discogs misses must leave _album_cache empty.\n\n<details><summary>Evidence</summary>\n\nExecuted repro (/tmp/repro_f13.py): with musicbrainzngs.search_releases raising NetworkError, 'get_cover_art_url during MB outage -> None'; after resolve() with both Discogs tiers cleanly missing: 'album cache after outage-resolve: (<MetadataSource.FALLBACK: 3>, None)'; then with MusicBrainz stubbed healthy and returning a real URL, the next track of the album still got 'cover_art_url: None (cache pinned the transient None)'.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Source: `CODE_REVIEW_2026-08-07.md` (repo root, gitignored — full report incl. dedup record, lens coverage notes, and the completeness-critic assessment)._",
