  {
   "finding_id": "gap2-1",
   "title": "[R4:gap2-1] discogs_live_check.py verifies only play_count_field_name; a misconfigured last_played_field_name passes every check green",
   "body": "_Round 4 cold audit (2026-08-07) · finding `gap2-1` · **Wave 4 — First boot: install path, operator tooling & token hygiene** · verdict **CONFIRMED** (executed reproduction) · severity **MEDIUM**_\n\n**Location:** `scripts/discogs_live_check.py:128`  \n**Lens:** Gap: Unowned operator tooling and test harness (discogs_live_check.py, conftest stub, factories, get_lastfm_session_key runtime)\n\n## Defect\nThe diagnostic exists to catch field-name mismatches before first play: check_collection_fields cross-checks client.play_count_field_name against the live field map and prints 'Check that play_count_field_name in config.yaml matches exactly (case-sensitive)' on a miss (lines 128-133). But the writer's OTHER production write — update_last_played — is never referenced anywhere in the script (grep for 'last_played' returns 0 hits). writer.last_played_field_name is sitting right there on the object the function already receives, and pi-setup-guide.md:173 explicitly warns the operator to 'set this to match its name exactly'. Neither the field-map check nor --test-write exercises the Last Played half, so the exact class of typo the script exists to catch sails through it for one of the two fields it writes.\n\n## Failure scenario\nOperator creates a 'Last Played' custom field in Discogs but writes last_played_field_name: \"Last played\" (case slip) in config.yaml. Runs `python scripts/discogs_live_check.py --test-write` per pi-setup-guide §9: every check prints green, Play Count increments, operator concludes Discogs is fully wired. In production, every session end logs \"Custom field 'Last played' not found\" and update_last_played returns False — Last Played is never recorded for any play, discoverable only by reading the journal, on an appliance the operator was told to verify with exactly this script.\n\n## Suggested fix\nIn check_collection_fields, mirror the play-count check for the last-played field: if client.last_played_field_name is set, mark it in the printed list ('← Last Played target') and fail() if it is not in fields (with the same case-sensitivity hint); print an info line if it is unconfigured. Optionally have --test-write also call writer.update_last_played (it writes today's date — same reset-manually caveat already printed for Play Count).\n\n## Verifier's fix note\nThe field-map mirror in check_collection_fields is the essential part and is sound (also update the existing marker text, since with two targets '← this is the one we update' becomes ambiguous — e.g. '← Play Count target' / '← Last Played target'). Two corrections to the optional --test-write extension: (1) update_last_played OVERWRITES the real last-played date with today's — unlike Play Count the old value is not 'reset manually' recoverable, so the printed caveat must say the previous date is lost, or the write test should be skipped for this field; (2) update_last_played returns False when clock_is_trustworthy() fails (pre-NTP boot — plausible during Pi bring-up, which is exactly when this script runs), so a False there must not be reported as a field-name failure; distinguish the two causes in the output. The field-map check alone already catches the typo class the finding describes, so the write extension is genuinely optional.\n\n<details><summary>Evidence</summary>\n\nscripts/discogs_live_check.py lines 124-133 handle only `client.play_count_field_name`; `grep -c \"last_played\" scripts/discogs_live_check.py` → 0. writer.py:63 exposes `self.last_played_field_name`; writer.py:203-208 logs 'Custom field ... not found' and returns False per write on mismatch. config.example.yaml:29-30 and pi-setup-guide.md:173 ('set this to match its name exactly') document the feature. Executed end-to-end stub run of main() with --test-write confirms the script never issues any Last-Played-related request (only POST .../fields/3 with {'value': '8'}).\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Source: `CODE_REVIEW_2026-08-07.md` (repo root, gitignored — full report incl. dedup record, lens coverage notes, and the completeness-critic assessment)._",
