  {
   "finding_id": "ops-2",
   "title": "[R4:ops-2] pi-setup-guide display config and screen blanking target the legacy X11/firmware stack; inert on every OS the guide's Imager step can flash (Trixie now, Bookworm as Legacy)",
   "body": "_Round 4 cold audit (2026-08-07) · finding `ops-2` · **Wave 4 — First boot: install path, operator tooling & token hygiene** · verdict **CONFIRMED** (executed reproduction) · severity **MEDIUM**_\n\n**Location:** `docs/pi-setup-guide.md:51`  \n**Lens:** Operability, config & Pi bring-up\n\n## Defect\nSection 3 (pi-setup-guide.md:51-62) configures the Waveshare panel's 1024×600 mode by editing `/boot/config.txt` and setting `hdmi_group=2 / hdmi_mode=87 / hdmi_cvt=1024 600 60 6 0 0 0 / hdmi_drive=1`. This is doubly inert on Bookworm and Trixie: (a) the boot config moved to `/boot/firmware/config.txt` — `/boot/config.txt` on fresh images is a stub whose only content is a do-not-edit notice, so `sudo nano /boot/config.txt` edits a file nothing reads; and (b) the `hdmi_*` firmware options are legacy-graphics-only and are ignored under the KMS driver (`dtoverlay=vc4-kms-v3d`), which has been the default since Bullseye and is the only supported stack on Bookworm/Trixie — under KMS the mode comes from EDID or a `video=HDMI-A-1:1024x600M@60D` entry in /boot/firmware/cmdline.txt. Section 13 (line 506-515) has the same staleness for screen blanking: `/etc/xdg/lxsession/LXDE-pi/autostart` does not exist on the default session (Wayfire on Bookworm-2023, labwc since late 2024 and on Trixie — both Wayland), and `@xset s off / -dpms / s noblank` only controls an X server, not the Wayland compositor's blanking (raspi-config's Screen Blanking toggle or the labwc/wayfire config is the operative knob). The Wayland default also makes the guide's `DISPLAY=:0 xrandr` verification (line 73) report an XWAYLAND virtual output and makes the systemd unit's `XAUTHORITY=/home/pi/.Xauthority` (line 352) point at a file that typically does not exist on a Wayland session.\n\n## Failure scenario\nFirst boot where the panel's EDID does not negotiate 1024×600 (the exact case §3 exists for): the operator edits /boot/config.txt as instructed, reboots, nothing changes, and every documented knob (hdmi_drive=2, checking for conflicting hdmi_mode lines in the Troubleshooting section, line 524-527) is equally inert — there is no working path to the right mode anywhere in the docs. Separately, on the always-on appliance: operator applies §13, the lxsession file is created but never read, xset never runs, and if the compositor's blanking is enabled the display goes dark mid-listening with the guide claiming blanking is disabled.\n\n## Suggested fix\nRewrite §3 for the KMS stack: check EDID first (`kmsprint` / the mode the desktop actually comes up in), and give the KMS fallback — `video=HDMI-A-1:1024x600M@60D` appended in `/boot/firmware/cmdline.txt` — instead of hdmi_cvt; all path references `/boot/firmware/config.txt`. Rewrite §13 for labwc/wayfire: `sudo raspi-config` → Display Options → Screen Blanking (off), with the X11 xset lines kept only as a footnote for users who switched the session to X11. Update the xrandr verification and the .Xauthority remark in §12/first-boot-checklist §0 to note the Wayland default (XAUTHORITY only applies to an X11 session).\n\n## Verifier's fix note\nThe suggested fix is correct; three refinements. (1) §3 should lead with the happy path: the Waveshare (H) panel has EDID and KMS normally negotiates 1024×600 with zero configuration — verify first (`kmsprint` or `wlr-randr` on the Wayland session; xrandr only reports XWAYLAND virtual outputs), and present `video=HDMI-A-1:1024x600M@60D` in /boot/firmware/cmdline.txt purely as the fallback. (2) The Troubleshooting entry at :524-527 must be rewritten in the same pass — the finding cites it but the fix list omits it; leaving it pointing at /boot/config.txt re-creates the dead end. (3) The systemd unit (:351-352) is a bigger issue than a footnote: on a labwc/Wayfire session, pygame/SDL2 launched by a system service with only DISPLAY=:0 and a nonexistent ~/.Xauthority may fail to connect at all (Xwayland auth), which turns this from a docs nit into \"the service doesn't start on a fresh flash\" — recommend verifying the unit on a current image and, if it fails, filing that separately as its own (likely HIGH) issue rather than folding it into this docs rewrite.\n\n<details><summary>Evidence</summary>\n\ndocs/pi-setup-guide.md:51 `sudo nano /boot/config.txt`; :56-62 the hdmi_group/hdmi_mode/hdmi_cvt/hdmi_drive block; :73 `DISPLAY=:0 xrandr | head -5`; :506 `sudo nano /etc/xdg/lxsession/LXDE-pi/autostart` with :512-514 `@xset s off/@xset -dpms/@xset s noblank`; :352 `Environment=\"XAUTHORITY=/home/pi/.Xauthority\"`. Target OS: requirements.txt:1 names Bookworm; the executed Imager-feed check (finding above) shows the guide's step-1 choice now flashes Trixie — both are KMS+Wayland releases with the boot config at /boot/firmware/config.txt. Raspberry Pi's own documentation marks hdmi_group/hdmi_mode/hdmi_cvt as legacy-display options not honoured by the KMS driver. Nothing in the repo or three audit rounds (closed_issues #1-#178, incl. the systemd-focused CRIT-4 #83) mentions Wayland, KMS, or the /boot/firmware move.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Source: `CODE_REVIEW_2026-08-07.md` (repo root, gitignored — full report incl. dedup record, lens coverage notes, and the completeness-critic assessment)._",
   "labels": [
    "code-review",
    "documentation",
    "severity:medium"
