  {
   "finding_id": "gap2-3",
   "title": "[R4:gap2-3] discogs_live_check.py resolves config.yaml from the CWD while resolving imports from the repo root — run from anywhere else it fails with the misleading 'Copy config.example.yaml' message",
   "body": "_Round 4 cold audit (2026-08-07) · finding `gap2-3` · **Wave 4 — First boot: install path, operator tooling & token hygiene** · verdict **CONFIRMED** (executed reproduction) · severity **LOW**_\n\n**Location:** `scripts/discogs_live_check.py:188`  \n**Lens:** Gap: Unowned operator tooling and test harness (discogs_live_check.py, conftest stub, factories, get_lastfm_session_key runtime)\n\n## Defect\nLine 183 computes the repo root (`Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent`) and uses it to fix sys.path so imports work from any CWD — but line 188 calls `load_config()` with its default CWD-relative 'config.yaml'. So the script is deliberately made location-independent for imports and left location-dependent for config. Run from anywhere but the repo root (e.g. `python vinyl-now-playing/scripts/discogs_live_check.py` from $HOME over SSH, or from inside scripts/), it exits with load_config's message 'config.yaml not found. Copy config.example.yaml to config.yaml and fill in your values.' — telling an operator who already has a filled-in config.yaml to create another one.\n\n## Failure scenario\nDuring bring-up the operator SSHes in and runs `python vinyl-now-playing/scripts/discogs_live_check.py` from their home directory. Imports succeed (sys.path fix), then the script prints '✗ config.yaml not found. Copy config.example.yaml to config.yaml and fill in your values.' The operator, whose config.yaml exists and works for the app, is sent debugging a config problem that is actually a CWD problem — the exact 'fails during first boot and sends the operator debugging the wrong layer' failure mode a diagnostic must not have.\n\n## Suggested fix\nThe repo root is already computed at line 183; reuse it: `root = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent; sys.path.insert(0, str(root)); ... config = load_config(str(root / 'config.yaml'))`. This cannot diverge from the app (main.py runs with WorkingDirectory=repo root, so both resolve the same file).\n\n## Verifier's fix note\nSuggested fix is correct as written: reuse the already-computed root — root = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent; sys.path.insert(0, str(root)); config = load_config(str(root / \"config.yaml\")). Side benefit: on genuine absence the ConfigError then prints the absolute path, making the message more diagnostic. Cannot diverge from the app since main.py runs with WorkingDirectory=repo root.\n\n<details><summary>Evidence</summary>\n\nscripts/discogs_live_check.py:183 `sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent))` vs :188 `config = load_config()`; src/config.py:394 `def load_config(path: str = 'config.yaml')` and :402-405 raise ConfigError \"{path} not found. Copy config.example.yaml to {path} and fill in your values.\" Repo root contains no config.yaml (gitignored), so the default path only resolves when CWD == repo root.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Source: `CODE_REVIEW_2026-08-07.md` (repo root, gitignored — full report incl. dedup record, lens coverage notes, and the completeness-critic assessment)._",
