  {
   "finding_id": "ops-4",
   "title": "[R4:ops-4] pi-setup-guide §8b/§8d (and the helper's own docstring) still describe the pre-S-3 \"prints session key to terminal\" behavior; script now writes a 0600 file",
   "body": "_Round 4 cold audit (2026-08-07) · finding `ops-4` · **Wave 4 — First boot: install path, operator tooling & token hygiene** · verdict **CONFIRMED** (executed reproduction) · severity **LOW**_\n\n**Location:** `docs/pi-setup-guide.md:215`  \n**Lens:** Operability, config & Pi bring-up\n\n## Defect\npi-setup-guide.md §8b step 4 (line 215) says the helper will \"Print your session key to the terminal\", and §8d (line 254) refers to values copied from \"the session key helper output\". The script stopped doing that when finding S-3 (#36) was fixed: get_lastfm_session_key.py now deliberately never echoes the key — it writes it to `lastfm_session_key.txt` with 0600 perms (get_lastfm_session_key.py:30, 81-97) and prints only the file path, telling the user to paste the file contents and then delete the file. The guide describing the pre-fix behavior undoes part of the point of the fix (an operator following the guide goes looking for the key in scrollback) and leaves the actual artifact — a credential file dropped in the repo root — undocumented in the setup flow (it is also not in .gitignore, though the script says to delete it).\n\n## Failure scenario\nOperator runs the helper over SSH per §8b, approves in the browser, presses Enter, and scans the terminal for the promised session key; the output instead names a file. Minor confusion at best; at worst the operator cats the file into the terminal (recreating the scrollback exposure S-3 removed) and leaves lastfm_session_key.txt sitting in the working tree of a git repo.\n\n## Suggested fix\nUpdate §8b step 4 to \"Write your session key to lastfm_session_key.txt (0600, owner-only)\", update §8d's wording, add a step to delete the file after pasting the value into config.yaml (mirroring the script's own final instruction), and add `lastfm_session_key.txt` to .gitignore as a belt-and-suspenders guard.\n\n## Verifier's fix note\nDrop the .gitignore step — lastfm_session_key.txt is already ignored (.gitignore lines 4-5). Keep the doc edits: §8b step 4 → \"Write your session key to lastfm_session_key.txt (0600, owner-only) and print its path\"; after \"Copy the session key into config.yaml\" add \"then delete lastfm_session_key.txt\"; §8d \"helper output\" → \"the file the session key helper wrote\". Additionally fix the same staleness in get_lastfm_session_key.py's module docstring (lines 3-4: \"paste the printed session key\") which the finding did not cite.\n\n<details><summary>Evidence</summary>\n\ndocs/pi-setup-guide.md:215 \"4. Print your session key to the terminal\"; :254 \"...the session key helper output\". get_lastfm_session_key.py:30 `_KEY_OUTPUT_FILE = \"lastfm_session_key.txt\"`; :81-97 writes via os.open(..., 0600) and never prints the key; :104 prints \"Your session key was written (0600, owner-only) to: <path>\"; :111-112 \"Then delete the file...\". Closed #36 (S-3) fixed the script; the guide's §8b/§8d text was never reconciled. `grep -n lastfm_session_key .gitignore` → no entry.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Source: `CODE_REVIEW_2026-08-07.md` (repo root, gitignored — full report incl. dedup record, lens coverage notes, and the completeness-critic assessment)._",
   "labels": [
    "code-review",
    "documentation",
    "severity:low"
