   "finding_id": "test-2",
   "title": "[R4:test-2] Retry helper's raise branch unpinned: a re-raise mutant in _finalize_write_with_retry passes 948/948, leaving the #163 raise-as-failure contract unguarded",
   "body": "_Round 4 cold audit (2026-08-07) · finding `test-2` · **Wave 6 — Test debt, mutation pins & doc drift** · verdict **CONFIRMED** (executed reproduction) · severity **MEDIUM**_\n\n**Location:** `src/tracking/listen_tracker.py:411`  \n**Lens:** Test-suite & docs quality\n\n## Defect\n_finalize_write_with_retry's docstring (lines 392-395) promises it retries 'treating BOTH a falsy result and a raised exception as a failure', but coverage shows lines 411-412 (`except Exception as e: log.warning(...)`) never execute. The suite exercises attempt()-returns-False retry (test_listen_tracker.py:357 `side_effect = [False, False, True]`) and the #171 raise-containment around update_last_played (line 1060), but no test ever makes increment_play_count RAISE — so the branch deciding whether a raising Play Count write is retried or aborts the credit is unpinned. This is the exact defect class #163 ('finalize write failure loses the previous record's Discogs credit, no retry') and #171 were filed to close.\n\n## Failure scenario\nA regression that narrows or removes the except clause (e.g. someone 'cleans up' the broad except, or adds a re-raise for a specific exception type) ships green. On the Pi, a Discogs 500/timeout that RAISES on the first increment attempt then propagates instead of being retried: the completed album's Play Count credit is lost with no retry — silently re-opening #163 for the raise case, on real collection data.\n\n## Suggested fix\nAdd two tests: (1) `writer.increment_play_count.side_effect = [RuntimeError('500'), True]` → assert session.credited is True and call_count == 2 (a raise counts as a failed attempt and is retried); (2) side_effect = RuntimeError on all attempts → assert _end_session completes without raising, credited stays False, and the 'LOST' error is logged.\n\n## Verifier's fix note\nSuggested tests verified verbatim: (1) increment_play_count.side_effect=[RuntimeError('500'), True] → session.credited is True, call_count == 2; (2) side_effect=RuntimeError on all attempts → _end_session completes, credited False, call_count == _FINALIZE_WRITE_ATTEMPTS. Both red on the mutant, green on current code. Implementation detail: reuse make_tracker() from tests/test_listen_tracker.py and patch src.tracking.listen_tracker.asyncio.sleep with AsyncMock (as the existing retry tests at :313/:339 do) so the 1s+2s backoff doesn't slow the suite. Optionally add caplog assertion on the 'attempt %d/%d raised' warning to pin the log line too, but the call_count + credited assertions are the load-bearing pins.\n\n<details><summary>Evidence</summary>\n\npytest --cov: 'src/tracking/listen_tracker.py 135 2 99% 411-412' — exactly the except clause. `grep -rn increment_play_count tests/` shows only False-returning side_effects, never an exception. Executed mutation in a /tmp copy: appended `raise` inside the except (raise propagates instead of retrying) → '948 passed, 1 warning in 6.10s'.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Source: `CODE_REVIEW_2026-08-07.md` (repo root, gitignored — full report incl. dedup record, lens coverage notes, and the completeness-critic assessment)._",
