   "finding_id": "test-3",
   "title": "[R4:test-3] Untested Discogs database tier + _build_result cover/label branches: triple mutation (tier deleted, image preference inverted, catno filter dropped) passes 948/948",
   "body": "_Round 4 cold audit (2026-08-07) · finding `test-3` · **Wave 6 — Test debt, mutation pins & doc drift** · verdict **CONFIRMED** (executed reproduction) · severity **MEDIUM**_\n\n**Location:** `src/metadata/discogs/reader.py:163`  \n**Lens:** Test-suite & docs quality\n\n## Defect\nThree related gaps, proven in one mutation run. (1) search_database (reader.py:163-182) — the tier that resolves EVERY album not in the operator's collection, including its try/skip-failed-candidate loop — has zero coverage; all seven test files that touch it mock it (the #49/T-4 remediation's test file docstring routes search_collection to test_discogs_search_errors.py and covers get_tracklist itself, but search_database was left out of both). (2) _build_result's cover_art_url extraction (360-364: primary-image preference, `.get(\"uri\")`) never executes because test_discogs_client.py's `_make_full_release` sets `images = []`. (3) Label/catno extraction incl. the Discogs `\"none\"` catalog-number filter (373-376) never executes (`labels = []`). test_discogs_search_errors.py additionally mocks `client._build_result` on the object under test. Related factory drift: test_resolver.py's make_discogs_result omits the `genres` key that the real _build_result always emits, so the resolver's genre pass-through is exercised only against a shape the producer never produces.\n\n## Failure scenario\nSimultaneously: search_database body replaced with `return None` (database tier deleted — every non-owned album silently falls to the MusicBrainz fallback with no year/label/catalog/tracklist), primary-image preference inverted plus `uri`→`resource_url` (wrong or missing cover for every multi-image release — the cover drives the entire palette/theming path), and the catno-'none' filter dropped (the literal string 'none' rendered as a catalog number on the card). Suite: fully green. Any one of these shipped as a refactor regression reaches the physical display unnoticed.\n\n## Suggested fix\nAdd tests with realistically-shaped Release mocks: search_database returning the first buildable candidate and skipping a candidate whose _build_result raises; _build_result with populated `images` (primary not first — assert primary wins and `uri` is read; no primary — assert images[0] fallback) and populated `labels` (assert label name, catno pass-through, and catno=='None' → None). Add `genres` to make_discogs_result to match the producer's shape.\n\n## Verifier's fix note\nThe suggested fix is correct and matches the code as written. Two additions: (a) the search_database tests should let the real _build_result run (or at least not mock it away) so the try/skip-failed-candidate loop at reader.py:175-180 is exercised end-to-end — the existing test_discogs_search_errors.py pattern of mocking _build_result on the object under test is fine for its write-target-selection purpose but must not be copied here; (b) the catno assertion should use the mixed-case string \"None\"/\"none\" both ways since the filter is .lower()-based (reader.py:376). The genres addition to make_discogs_result is cosmetic-but-correct: resolver.py:204 uses .get() so no behavior is currently at risk; frame it as shape-parity, not a bug fix. Note the tracklist leg of _build_result IS covered (get_tracklist has its own tests and _build_result tests mock it), so scope the new tests to images/labels only.\n\n<details><summary>Evidence</summary>\n\npytest --cov: 'src/metadata/discogs/reader.py 152 27 82% 78, 171-182, ... 360-366, 373-378 ...'. tests/test_discogs_client.py:1011-1018: `release.images = []; release.labels = []`. Executed triple mutation in a /tmp copy (search_database → `return None`; `== \"primary\"` → `!=` and `uri` → `resource_url`; catno filter dropped) → '948 passed, 1 warning in 5.02s'.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Source: `CODE_REVIEW_2026-08-07.md` (repo root, gitignored — full report incl. dedup record, lens coverage notes, and the completeness-critic assessment)._",
