   "finding_id": "gap3-2",
   "title": "[R4:gap3-2] SEC-4's _DOWNLOAD_DEADLINE_SECONDS and PCONC-2's _RECOGNIZE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS lack MUT-9-style shipped-value pins — both mutable to 10^9 with 948/948 green (executed)",
   "body": "_Round 4 cold audit (2026-08-07) · finding `gap3-2` · **Wave 6 — Test debt, mutation pins & doc drift** · verdict **CONFIRMED** (executed reproduction) · severity **LOW**_\n\n**Location:** `src/display/cover_cache.py:101`  \n**Lens:** Gap: Closed-issue regression sweep: do the 178 closures still hold in v1.5.7?\n\n## Defect\nThe #119 closure's CHANGELOG entry claims 'Pinned every numeric limit in the fetch and rate-limit paths to its shipped value (MUT-9, #119)' and enumerates _MAX_COVER_BYTES, _MAX_COVER_REDIRECTS, _COVER_CONNECT_READ_TIMEOUT, _HTTP_TIMEOUT, _RATE_LIMIT_MAX_WAIT, _RATE_LIMIT_DEFAULT_WAIT. It omits _DOWNLOAD_DEADLINE_SECONDS — the total-wall-clock budget that IS the SEC-4 slow-drip control in the very same download path, and arguably the most security-relevant numeric in the file. Mutating it to 10**9 passes 948/948. The deadline's own tests exhibit the #164 pattern in miniature: test_cover_cache.py:703 and :822 monkeypatch the constant to 45 (its intended value) before exercising the mechanism, so the mechanism is proven while the shipped value is free to drift (a units slip like `45 * 1000`, or a revert to no-deadline-in-practice, ships green). The same holds for the PCONC-2/#100 bound: _RECOGNIZE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS = 30 (src/audio/recognizer.py:37) mutated to 10**9 also passes 948/948 — the one test of the timeout path (test_recognizer.py:603) injects `loop.recognize_timeout = 0.05` itself. Setting either constant to effectively-infinite is a behavioral revert of its closure (a hung Shazam call re-occupies the recognition loop for minutes; a slow-drip cover fetch re-parks an executor worker), yet the suite cannot see it.\n\n## Failure scenario\nA future edit (units refactor, 'temporarily' raising a timeout while debugging, or an accidental revert) changes _DOWNLOAD_DEADLINE_SECONDS or _RECOGNIZE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS to a value that no longer bounds anything. Suite stays 948/948 green, CI passes, the change ships. On the Pi, a degraded shazamio call once again occupies the recognition loop past queue saturation (the pre-PCONC-2 failure), or a dripping cover response parks a shared-pool worker for the drip's duration (the pre-SEC-4 failure) — the exact behaviors #100 and the SEC-4 fix closed.\n\n## Suggested fix\nAdd the two shipped-value assertions in the same style #119 used for the constants it did pin: `assert cc._DOWNLOAD_DEADLINE_SECONDS == 45` (beside the existing `assert cc._MAX_COVER_REDIRECTS == 5` at test_cover_cache.py:940) and `assert _RECOGNIZE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS == 30` in test_recognizer.py; optionally also pin _SHAZAM_RETRY_ATTEMPTS/_SHAZAM_RETRY_MAX_TIMEOUT_SECONDS, the other PCONC-2 numerics.\n\n## Verifier's fix note\nThe suggested fix is correct and cheap. Refinements: (1) add `assert cc._DOWNLOAD_DEADLINE_SECONDS == 45` inside the existing test_cover_fetch_constants_are_the_shipped_values (test_cover_cache.py:934), which is the pin test the MUT-9 closure created, rather than merely 'beside line 940'; (2) add `assert _RECOGNIZE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS == 30` in test_recognizer.py, and consider also asserting the seeding link (`RecognitionLoop(...).recognize_timeout == _RECOGNIZE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` or equivalent), since test_recognizer.py:603 overrides the instance attribute — pinning the constant alone would not catch a regression that stops recognizer.py:239 from using it; (3) do not reword the #119 CHANGELOG entry — it was accurate when written (the deadline postdates it); if anything, note the pin extension under the new entry. Optionally pin _SHAZAM_RETRY_* as suggested, same pattern.\n\n<details><summary>Evidence</summary>\n\nMutation runs in a /tmp copy (baseline 948 green): 'M35-MUT9-deadline-inf: SURVIVED — 948 passed' (_DOWNLOAD_DEADLINE_SECONDS = 45 → 10**9) and 'M34-MUT9-recognize-timeout-inf: SURVIVED — 948 passed' (_RECOGNIZE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS = 30 → 10**9). Contrast: the neighboring constants ARE pinned — 'M36-MUT9-cover-bytes-inf: killed' and test_cover_cache.py:940 'assert cc._MAX_COVER_REDIRECTS == 5'. test_cover_cache.py:703/:822: 'monkeypatch.setattr(cc, \"_DOWNLOAD_DEADLINE_SECONDS\", 45)' — the test sets the value it should be verifying. CHANGELOG.md:1021-1024 states the 'every numeric limit in the fetch and rate-limit paths' claim.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Source: `CODE_REVIEW_2026-08-07.md` (repo root, gitignored — full report incl. dedup record, lens coverage notes, and the completeness-critic assessment)._",
   "labels": [
