  {
   "finding_id": "gap3-3",
   "title": "[R4:gap3-3] B-22/STAB-5 decode-path _cover_version bump (renderer.py:1490) is unpinned: mutation to `pass` survives 948/948",
   "body": "_Round 4 cold audit (2026-08-07) · finding `gap3-3` · **Wave 6 — Test debt, mutation pins & doc drift** · verdict **CONFIRMED** (executed reproduction) · severity **LOW**_\n\n**Location:** `src/display/renderer.py:1490`  \n**Lens:** Gap: Closed-issue regression sweep: do the 178 closures still hold in v1.5.7?\n\n## Defect\nThe B-22 fix replaced the GC-collidable id(cover) static-frame cache key with a monotonic `_cover_version` that must be bumped wherever a cover 'lands'. There are two bump sites: the prefetch path (renderer.py:1362, download+palette landed) and the async decode path (renderer.py:1490, `_decode_cover_async` — the STAB-5 off-loop SD-read/decode that EVERY rendered cover passes through). Mutating the 1490 bump to `pass` survives the full suite (948/948). In the common flow the miss is masked: the 1s palette lerp keeps changing the static key each frame, so a decode landing within ~1s gets recomposed anyway. But the cases this bump exists for are exactly the ones outside that window: a worn-SD decode that takes seconds (the STAB-5 scenario the docstring names — 'the step that can stall for SECONDS on a worn card'), a deferred decode recovering after a transient display fault (`_cover_decode_deferred`), or reduced_motion where the palette snaps in one frame. In all of those, without the bump the decoded cover sits in `_cover_cache` while `_static_key` never changes, so the cached no-cover frame is blitted until the next track/state change — the user-visible symptom B-22's stable-token design was shipped to prevent. The behavior is real today but guarded by nothing; per this project's own standard, a fix whose reversion passes 948/948 is unpinned.\n\n## Failure scenario\nA refactor of `_decode_cover_async` (e.g. the v1.6 idle-screen work touching the cover pipeline) drops or reorders the version bump. Suite green, ships. On the Pi with a slow SD read or reduced_motion enabled, every track change shows the placeholder for the whole track even though the cover decoded successfully moments after the palette settled; the STAB-1 deferred-recovery path likewise repaints nothing after HDMI recovery.\n\n## Suggested fix\nAdd a test that drives `_decode_cover_async` to a successful decode (existing renderer tests already stub pygame) with the palette settled, and asserts `_cover_version` increased (or that a subsequent `_render_now_playing` recomposes with the cover — key change observable via `_static_key`). Mirror whatever pin covers the 1362 prefetch bump.\n\n## Verifier's fix note\nCheapest pin: add `assert r._cover_version == 1` (and `r._dirty is True`) to the existing successful-decode tests — test_stab1_deferred_flag_clears_when_display_returns and/or the B-18 corrupt-then-heal test in tests/test_renderer_robustness.py — which already drive _decode_cover_async to a clean decode with a video mode set (make_renderer already initializes _cover_version = 0). That mirrors the 1362 pin without new fixture work. Asserting _cover_version directly is preferable to asserting a _static_key change, which would require standing up the full render path and could be masked by palette-lerp key churn.\n\n<details><summary>Evidence</summary>\n\nMutation run in a /tmp copy: 'M24-B22-version-no-bump: SURVIVED (unpinned!) — 948 passed, 1 warning in 4.85s' (renderer.py:1490 `self._cover_version += 1` → `pass`; the `self._dirty = True` beside it left intact, so redraws still occur — they just reuse the stale cached frame because the key at renderer.py:587 `self._cover_version,  # bumps when a cover lands (stable; no id() reuse — B-22)` never changes). The sibling bump at 1362 is exercised (same mutation there was not attempted against a green suite claim; the 1490 path is the one every decoded cover traverses per `_load_cover` → `_decode_cover_async`).\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Source: `CODE_REVIEW_2026-08-07.md` (repo root, gitignored — full report incl. dedup record, lens coverage notes, and the completeness-critic assessment)._",
   "labels": [
    "code-review",
    "testing",
    "severity:low"
   ],
   "milestone_title": "Wave 6 — Test debt, mutation pins & doc drift"
