  {
   "finding_id": "test-4",
   "title": "[R4:test-4] README.md:24 and architecture.md:834 document acrcloud/audd as valid recognition.backend values that config.py's CRIT-2 gate rejects at startup (config.example.yaml alone was reconciled by #93)",
   "body": "_Round 4 cold audit (2026-08-07) · finding `test-4` · **Wave 6 — Test debt, mutation pins & doc drift** · verdict **CONFIRMED** (executed reproduction) · severity **LOW**_\n\n**Location:** `README.md:24`  \n**Lens:** Test-suite & docs quality\n\n## Defect\nREADME.md:24 lists '🔧 Swappable recognition backend (ShazamIO, ACRCloud, AudD)' as a current feature, and docs/architecture.md:834's configuration-reference row for `recognition.backend` documents the value domain as `\"shazamio\" | \"acrcloud\" | \"audd\"`. Since the #93 (CRIT-2) fix, src/config.py:287 `IMPLEMENTED_BACKENDS = frozenset({\"shazamio\"})` rejects both other values with an aggregated ConfigError at startup ('must be one of ['shazamio']'). config.example.yaml:60-62 was reconciled by that fix ('selecting them is rejected at startup until they are built') but these two doc surfaces were not — the architecture doc's own config table now documents values its own config layer rejects.\n\n## Failure scenario\nAn operator with an ACRCloud account reads either doc, sets `backend: \"acrcloud\"`, and gets a startup ConfigError telling them the documented value is invalid — the docs promise a feature the code deliberately refuses. Under the systemd unit this is a clean failure, but the contradiction is exactly the doc/code invariant drift the doc audits exist to catch.\n\n## Suggested fix\nREADME: '(ShazamIO today; ACRCloud/AudD planned)'. architecture.md table row: `\"shazamio\"` (only implemented backend; acrcloud/audd reserved in config.example.yaml but rejected at startup — CRIT-2).\n\n## Verifier's fix note\nSuggested fixes are correct as written. One addition the finding missed in the same class: src/audio/recognizer.py:4's module docstring also claims 'ACRCloud, or AudD can be swapped via config without touching this file' — present tense for an unimplemented capability; worth amending to 'planned' in the same commit (its line 291 TODO already frames them correctly).\n\n<details><summary>Evidence</summary>\n\nREADME.md:24 in the current-features bullet list; docs/architecture.md:834 `| recognition.backend | \"shazamio\" | \"shazamio\" \\| \"acrcloud\" \\| \"audd\" |`; src/config.py:287 `IMPLEMENTED_BACKENDS = frozenset({\"shazamio\"})` and the _check at config.py:318-320; config.example.yaml:60-62 already corrected.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Source: `CODE_REVIEW_2026-08-07.md` (repo root, gitignored — full report incl. dedup record, lens coverage notes, and the completeness-critic assessment)._",
