   "finding_id": "test-5",
   "title": "[R4:test-5] DisplayRenderer.run() (lines 519-541) has zero coverage: QUIT/ESC stop paths, dirty-reset ordering, and 30/10fps cadence all unpinned",
   "body": "_Round 4 cold audit (2026-08-07) · finding `test-5` · **Wave 6 — Test debt, mutation pins & doc drift** · verdict **CONFIRMED** (executed reproduction) · severity **LOW**_\n\n**Location:** `src/display/renderer.py:517`  \n**Lens:** Test-suite & docs quality\n\n## Defect\nCoverage shows renderer.py lines 519-541 (the whole body of `async def run()`) never execute. The suite tests _render dispatch, lifecycle wiring, palette, caches and perf, but never drives the loop itself: the pygame QUIT / K_ESCAPE stop() paths, the `transitioning` window computation, the deliberate 'reset self._dirty BEFORE rendering so a render can request another frame' ordering (the mechanism behind the P-3 'goes quiet at steady state' behavior architecture.md documents), and the 1/30-vs-1/10 sleep cadence are all unpinned. This is the same class as the closed TQ-2 (#137, main()) and TQ-7 (#138, capture.run()) findings — the renderer's loop was never picked up by either.\n\n## Failure scenario\nFlipping the dirty-reset to AFTER _render() (a natural-looking 'fix' during a refactor) makes animation frames self-cancel — the pulsing dot and palette lerp freeze at steady state — with the suite green; likewise a regression in the transitioning window (e.g. `>` vs `<`) would either pin the loop at 30fps forever (Pi CPU burn, the exact P-3 regression) or kill the 1s lerp, and nothing fails.\n\n## Suggested fix\nUnder the SDL dummy driver, run() is drivable: start it as a task, post a pygame.QUIT / KEYDOWN-ESC event and assert the task returns with _running False; set _dirty and a fresh _transition_start and assert flip() was called and the sleep interval selected 1/30 vs 1/10 (patch asyncio.sleep to capture the argument and stop the loop).\n\n## Verifier's fix note\nThe suggested fix works as written with one amendment: DisplayRenderer.stop() calls pygame.quit() (renderer.py:1526), so each loop-driving test case needs its own renderer + start() (and a pygame.display.quit()/re-init between cases) — a single renderer cannot be reused across the QUIT, ESC, and cadence sub-tests. For cadence capture, patching asyncio.sleep at the module level (src.display.renderer's asyncio) works cleanly; have the capturing sleep call r.stop() after N captures to end the loop, and note the loop exits via the while condition (not return), so the pygame.event.get() call on the next iteration after an external stop() would raise 'video system not initialized' — stop via the sleep hook before the next poll, or post an event instead.\n\n<details><summary>Evidence</summary>\n\npytest --cov: 'src/display/renderer.py 650 39 94% 519-541, ...' — 519-541 is exactly run()'s body (verified against the source). tests/test_renderer_lifecycle.py contains only init/start/dispatch/injection tests (grep 'def test' → 4 tests, none drive run()).\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Source: `CODE_REVIEW_2026-08-07.md` (repo root, gitignored — full report incl. dedup record, lens coverage notes, and the completeness-critic assessment)._",
